WEBVTT


00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.300
Should you move to Korea or Japan?

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:04.981
I lived in Tokyo for one year and now I live in Seoul.

00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:06.541
And here's my honest opinion.

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:08.941
First, I'm not saying one city is better than the other.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.701
I think it depends on your personality and what kind of life you want.

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:15.541
For cost, Tokyo is more expensive than Seoul. Food,

00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:18.381
transportation, daily life added up really fast.

00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:19.261
But I lived in the dorm

00:00:19.262 --> 00:00:21.681
so I didn't have to worry too much about the rent.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.280
In Seoul, monthly rent can look cheaper,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.780
but the deposit is usually high.

00:00:26.781 --> 00:00:28.941
So even if the rent looks okay,

00:00:28.942 --> 00:00:32.181
you still have to have that money upfront for daily life.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:35.561
Tokyo felt easier as a foreigner who doesn't speak the language.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.660
First of all, the environment is of course better.

00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:41.541
It was cleaner, quieter and more organized.

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:43.021
People usually follow the rules,

00:00:43.022 --> 00:00:45.121
line up proper, stay quiet in public.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.580
Even if you don't speak the language,

00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:48.961
they are always being polite. Like

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.260
as an introvert,

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:56.221
I really like Japan because eating alone felt very normal there.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.321
But sometimes Japan felt a little bit too polite.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.140
People were nice,

00:01:00.141 --> 00:01:03.461
but I could not really tell if they really wanted to be close

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.461
or they are just being polite.

00:01:05.462 --> 00:01:07.981
And so it feels different is faster,

00:01:07.982 --> 00:01:10.661
louder and more intense. When my career was not good,

00:01:10.662 --> 00:01:14.781
I felt more nervous going outside because some people can be impatient

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:16.621
and some restaurants like Korean Barbecues,

00:01:16.622 --> 00:01:19.161
you have to order. At least like two portions.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.980
So I felt kind of weird to go alone.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:25.501
So usually I don't. But now they are getting more and more.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:28.361
Like one person said to me,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.760
yeah, it's changing.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.820
But emotionally I feel like Korea fits me more.

00:01:32.821 --> 00:01:33.541
It's like, um,

00:01:33.542 --> 00:01:36.861
in Korea, once someone sees you as their friends,

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:39.981
they treat you so warmly, like they are loyal

00:01:39.982 --> 00:01:43.781
and they really treat you like you are their tong San or onnie, nunah,

00:01:43.782 --> 00:01:46.261
whatever, can actually like feel closer to them.

00:01:46.262 --> 00:01:49.861
The friendship feels more direct and close for me,

00:01:49.862 --> 00:01:53.941
um, Tokyo gave me comfort and Seoul gave me connection.

00:01:53.942 --> 00:01:56.581
I personally love traveling to Japan or living.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.001
I would still choose Korea.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:58.840
That's why I'm still here.
